          }
        ],
        "student_prefix_sha256": "844957e0ffafb23b75b9947b4f477417a6ff47ec36f51a25beb5a6e2c5078cb1",
        "target": "Initially, Kiaan has to deliver to 200 homes. After an hour, he has distributed newspapers to \\( \\frac{2}{5} \\) of the homes. So, the number of homes he has already delivered to is \\( \\frac{2}{5} \\times 200 = 80 \\) homes. This leaves \\( 200 - 80 = 120 \\) homes remaining.\n\nAfter another 2 hours, he has distributed newspapers to 60 percent of the remaining 120 homes. So, the number of homes he has delivered to in these 2 hours is \\( 0.60 \\times 120 = 72 \\) homes. This leaves \\( 120 - 72 = 48 \\) homes still needing newspapers.\n\nFINAL: 48",
